Z||000014||Leadfoot||07-25-2001||02:22 PM||||Hey Aus, did you spray paint your trunklid switch silver or did you have it coated?  Looks really nice! <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||AusFiero||07-25-2001||07:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR><B>Hey Aus, did you spray paint your trunklid switch silver or did you have it coated?  Looks really nice! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I painted all my switches and vents silver Leadfoot, and the dash bolts. For a good result you wipe them over with a damp (not to damp or wet) thinners rag befor painting. It softens the old plastic and the paint bites in real well. I used Acrylic. Holden Silver Fox Colour and a good coat of clear. They are standing up to useage very well.  The vents also come apart really easy for ease of painting. The switches also disassemble easily. Took a long time to do it all but was worth the effort. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000016||Joe Torma||07-25-2001||07:56 PM||||I will be working on guages for my Fiero.  Most likely silver faced...speedo will go up to 220mph with purple lighting(to match my paint color).  If it works out well, I can produce them.<P>I'll be able to use any font you want and almost any color face/backlight.<P>I've done some prelimnary tests and so far so good.<P>Joe<BR>||||reg||1
